# Platform configuration: current source inventory

This is a source inventory for CONFIG F1, not a migration or runtime acceptance.
The historical 1,374-entry discovery list has no entries whose source is
`skills/common/plugin-runtime/foundation/config/platform.ts`. Its search count
therefore cannot establish coverage of this shared configuration boundary.
The table below covers all 15 top-level properties in the current
[schema](../../../../skills/common/plugin-runtime/foundation/config/platform.schema.json).
Nested plugin settings remain to be inventoried separately.

[Source identities and schema coverage](../../evidence/config-platform-inventory-20260921/source-inventory.json)
bind the inspected files to the current uncommitted tree; the same evidence
directory retains the tracked source patch and the new Buster consumer source.
This is an inventory snapshot, not a new runtime test result.

The [independent source review](independent-config-platform-inventory-20260921.md)
accepts this bounded inventory, including its schema coverage, consumer paths
and explicit unresolved nested settings. CONFIG F1–F6 remain incomplete.

## Author and loading paths

[loadPlatformConfig](../../../../skills/common/plugin-runtime/foundation/config/platform.ts)
reads a separately selected `pipeline-platform.v2` JSON file. It resolves the
real file path, validates the complete object with the existing schema, resolves
installation/trusted/storage/isolation paths relative to that real file's parent,
and recursively freezes the returned configuration. It does not currently derive
these settings from `swarm.config.json`.

Nova's [core CLI](../../../../skills/nova/core/cli.ts),
[project CLI](../../../../skills/nova/project/cli.ts), and
[legacy-import CLI](../../../../skills/nova/project/legacy-import-cli.ts) select
the file through `--platform`. Buster's
[runtimeRegistry](../../../../skills/buster/engine/test-gates/production-config-values.ts)
selects it through the separate remote configuration's `platformConfig` field,
resolved relative to that configuration's directory. Buster uses the loaded
installation and trust settings to discover its registry; this does not prove
that Buster consumes every Nova platform setting.

## Field classification and actual consumers

All required fields have no default in this loader. Optional fields are marked
explicitly. The existing selected JSON file is the current author for operator
values; central migration and rejection/removal of that competing author remain
pending.

| Field | Type/unit and classification | Actual consumer / current default |
|---|---|---|
| `schemaVersion` | Fixed protocol identity `pipeline-platform.v2` | Schema validation; protocol invariant, not an operator tuning setting. |
| `installationRoots` | Nonempty unique string array; installation selection | Nova `prepareRuntime` and Buster `runtimeRegistry` → `discoverPackages`; paths resolved relative to the real config file. |
| `trustedBuiltinRoots` | Nonempty unique string array; operator trust boundary | Both discovery paths' trust policy; resolved paths, no fallback. |
| `externalTrust.allowedSourceDigests` | Map of source identifiers to nonempty unique SHA-256 arrays; trust policy | Both discovery paths → `allowedSourceDigests` Map. These are digest values, not secret material. |
| `externalTrust.verifiedAttestations` | SHA-256-keyed map to SHA-256 values; trust evidence binding | Both discovery paths → `verifiedAttestations` Map. Migration must preserve the existing verification meaning. |
| `providers` | Map of capability identifiers to provider strings; operator selection | Nova `prepareRuntime` → `resolveCapabilityGrants`; no local provider default in this loader. |
| `grants` | Nested capability configuration objects; operator capability policy | Nova `prepareRuntime` → `resolveCapabilityGrants`. Nested keys require the capability contracts, not a blanket central passthrough. |
| `adapters` | Map of adapter configuration objects; plugin-specific operator settings | Nova registration configuration validation, `AdapterRuntime`, and selected Wait resolver root binding. Nested setting inventory remains open. |
| `activeAdapters` | Unique string array; operator activation policy | Nova `enabledRegistrations`; explicit selection is distinct from merely supplying adapter configuration. |
| `observers` | Map of observer configuration objects; plugin-specific operator settings | Nova enabled registrations, configuration validation, and observer runtime. Nested setting inventory remains open. |
| `isolation.cgroupRoot` | Optional nonempty path; operator host resource boundary | Resolved by loader, then Nova `activateRegistry`. Absence is preserved; this loader introduces no cgroup fallback. |
| `storageRoot` | Nonempty path; operator durable-state location | Nova run roots, resource-lock manager and retained Wait owner context; resolved relative to the real config file. |
| `shutdownTimeoutMs` | Required positive integer, milliseconds; operator lifecycle budget | Nova `AdapterRuntime` invocation shutdown and adapter startup/readiness/teardown timeouts. Schema currently has no upper bound; a migration must not silently invent or remove a bound. |
| `effectLockTtlMs` | Optional integer, 60,000–86,400,000 milliseconds; operator effect-lock lifetime | Nova `engine-runtime.ts` passes this to `EffectCoordinator`, with the current local fallback **300,000 ms**. That fallback is a remaining migration target. |
| `orchestratorIssuerId` | Nonempty string; operator authority identity | Nova decisions, recovery, signal history and retained Wait resolution. This is an identity binding, not merely a display label. |
| `administrativeDecisionIssuers` | Unique array of `{type,id}`; operator authority allowlist | Nova `engine-admin.ts` permits only matching operator/administrator principals for administrative reopening. |

`externalTrust` occupies one top-level schema property and has two separately
classified leaves above; likewise `isolation` is listed by its sole leaf. The
result is 16 table rows covering 15 top-level properties. This table does not
classify arbitrary nested plugin fields by inference.

The principal Nova consumer is
[engine-runtime.ts](../../../../skills/nova/core/execution/engine-runtime.ts);
administrative authority is enforced in
[engine-admin.ts](../../../../skills/nova/core/execution/engine-admin.ts).
This inventory records current source behavior only. It does not replace two
profile tests, actual CLI/consumer checks, invalid-input and old-author rejection,
or the independent F1–F6/DOC acceptance required for a central migration.
